* Auto-bridge subcircuit for the "74hct" family, digital output.
* Support file for auto-bridge-family-file-case.cir and
* auto-bridge-family-file-case-lower.cir.  The auto-bridge builds this file's
* name as bridge_<family>_<node type>_<direction>.subcir and resolves it with
* inp_pathresolve(), so the name here is the lower-case spelling that a deck
* writing family='74HCT' must reach in every casemode.
* The port order is the one the generated X card uses: digital node first,
* analogue node second.  See the commentary at
* src/xspice/evt/evtcheck_nodes.c:156-170.
.subckt bridge_74hct_d_out dig ana vcc=3.3
.model hct_dac dac_bridge(out_low = 0 out_high = '0.8 * vcc')
adac [ dig ] [ ana ] hct_dac
.ends
